== 6. Small derived figures (inputs are recorded measurements; arithmetic only)
   idle minion rail per shire at 73 C: 0.325 W (11.05 W / 34 shires; no firmware power gating)
   idle board power outside the minion clock domain (off-rail + NoC rail; the SRAM rail's shire caches share the minion clock, errata 2.30): 59% (18.74 W of 31.79 W)
   0.18.0 law at 300 MHz: minion 440 mV, SRAM 690 mV (if its governor acted; card 1's is inactive)
   0.18.0 law at 200 MHz: minion 420 mV, SRAM 670 mV (if its governor acted; card 1's is inactive)
   0.18.0 law at 100 MHz: minion 400 mV, SRAM 650 mV (if its governor acted; card 1's is inactive)
